<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7736d9e8-fff5-5bfc-96c2-edfdce1b9d54" activityNameId="f5f32c64-2aa6-58cb-8eb0-a10e1e5e071c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, spoil from coal mining, in surface landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, spoil from coal mining, in surface landfill
na;
Synonyms: coal mine overburden, coal mine waste rock; 
UUID: 36fc181c-13da-4792-aa29-e2012c405ccd
Waste-specific emissions from lignite spoil leachate. Short- and long-term emissions to groundwater from rainwater infiltration leaching. Leaching by lateral groundwater flow not included.; Geography: Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of coal spoil production in the world.
Location:  Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of coal spoil production in the world.
Technology: Mechanically stable and revegetated coal spoil backfill or heap.
Time period: Average coal spoil composition and leachate concentrations adopted from available lignite spoil data from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective model, specific to coal spoil sites.
Production volume: Approx. 22'240 Mio t/a spoil tailings generation
Sampling: Disposal model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial spoil composition from various literature sources.  
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_36fc181c-13da-4792-aa29-e2012c405ccd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">GLO</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location:  Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of coal spoil production in the world.</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: Mechanically stable and revegetated coal spoil backfill or heap.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
      <timePeriod startDate="1985-01-01" endDate="2009-12-31" isDataValidForEntirePeriod="true">
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Time period: Average coal spoil composition and leachate concentrations adopted from available lignite spoil data from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective model, specific to coal spoil sites.</text>
        </comment>
      </timePeriod>
